## Project Harness for GitHub Copilot

Follow `AGENTS.md` as the canonical repository workflow. Before changing files, run `node .harness/run.mjs session` and inspect `.harness/continuity.json`; run a pending `node .harness/run.mjs resume <handoff-id>` only from a genuinely fresh Copilot chat or task. Then read the small `.harness/` state files and run `doctor`, `status`, and `next`. Use the checked-in runtime for feature transitions and require successful `verify` evidence before completion. Use bounded checkpoints, and treat dirty-safe `handoff` plus `STOP_CURRENT_CHAT` as terminal. Compaction is not a substitute; the platform must create the next chat or task.
